.Dd October 24, 2026
.Dt SKYPLUG 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm skyplug
.Nd inspect and toggle Skyrim Special Edition plugins on Linux
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -game-dir Ar dir
.Op Fl -prefix Ar dir
.Op Fl -appid Ar appid
.Ar command
.Op Ar args
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads and edits the
.Pa Plugins.txt
load order of a Skyrim Special Edition install running under Proton or
Wine, Steam's or GOG's, without a mod manager.
It scans the game's
.Pa Data
directory for
.Pa .esp ,
.Pa .esm
and
.Pa .esl
files, cross-references them with
.Pa Plugins.txt
and
.Pa Skyrim.ccc ,
and reports what the engine will actually load.
.Pp
It can also read
.Pa .ess
save files directly, to show which characters exist, which saves belong
to each, and which plugins were active when a save was made.
.Ss What loads
Only two kinds of plugin load regardless of
.Pa Plugins.txt :
.Bl -bullet -width Ds
.It
the base game and DLC masters:
.Pa Skyrim.esm ,
.Pa Update.esm ,
.Pa Dawnguard.esm ,
.Pa HearthFires.esm
and
.Pa Dragonborn.esm ;
.It
Creation Club content listed in
.Pa Skyrim.ccc .
.El
.Pp
Every other plugin, including mod
.Pa .esm
files and
.Pa .esp
files carrying the master flag, loads only when it is prefixed with
.Ql *
in
.Pa Plugins.txt .
The master flag in a plugin's header only affects where it loads:
masters load ahead of regular plugins.
.Pp
The load order
.Nm
shows is an approximation: base game masters in their fixed order, then
Creation Club content in
.Pa Skyrim.ccc
order, then active masters, then active regular plugins, each group in
.Pa Plugins.txt
order.
The engine additionally sorts masters by their dependencies, which
.Nm
does not parse.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm list
List every plugin in
.Pa Data ,
plus any listed in
.Pa Plugins.txt
that no longer exist, each with a status marker:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width "[CC]" -compact
.It Li [x]
enabled in
.Pa Plugins.txt
.It Li [\ ]
present in
.Pa Data
but not enabled
.It Li [!]
listed in
.Pa Plugins.txt
but missing from
.Pa Data
.It Li [M]
base game/DLC master, always loaded
.It Li [CC]
Creation Club content, always loaded
.El
.It Cm enable Ar plugin
Enable
.Ar plugin
by setting its
.Ql *
prefix in
.Pa Plugins.txt ,
adding it to the end of the file if it is not listed yet.
.It Cm disable Ar plugin
Disable
.Ar plugin
by removing its
.Ql *
prefix.
A plugin not listed in
.Pa Plugins.txt
is left alone.
.It Cm edit
Open the interactive editor; see
.Sx EDITOR .
.It Cm paths
Print the resolved
.Pa Data ,
.Pa Plugins.txt ,
.Pa Skyrim.ccc
and saves paths, then exit.
Useful for checking that auto-detection found the right install.
.It Cm characters
List every character across all saves, with the number of saves each has
and details of the most recent one.
.It Cm saves Ar character
List every save belonging to
.Ar character .
.It Cm save-plugins Ar save
List the plugins that were active when
.Ar save
was made, each marked against the current setup with the same markers as
.Cm list .
.It Cm armours Op Ar plugin Op Fl -filter Ar text Op Fl -check
Without
.Ar plugin ,
list the plugins in the load order that have armour records, with how many.
With one, list its armours: name, editor ID, the slots it covers, and the models it is worn as
(for a female character, the human races), as the load order wears it: the last plugin that
changes an armature decides, so a plugin that refits vanilla armours shows the refitted models.
An armour a plugin only changes is marked with the plugin that adds it.
.Fl -filter
keeps armours whose name or editor ID contains
.Ar text .
.Fl -check
also reads each armour's models and flags with an exclamation mark
any the game won't draw: a skinned model records which slot each skin partition belongs to,
and the game only draws a partition whose slot is among the slots of the armature wearing it,
so moving an armour to another slot in its plugin without moving its model makes it
invisible.
.Cm preview Fl -armour
warns about the same.
.It Cm preview Ar model Op Fl o | Fl -out Ar file Op Fl -views Ar list Op Fl -size Ar pixels Op Fl -body Op Fl -with Ar model Op Fl -elevation Ar degrees Op Fl -zoom Ar factor Op Fl -transparent Op Fl -no-pose
Draw
.Ar model
with its textures and write a PNG with the views side by side, and print where each
texture came from (the loose file or archive the game uses, what it hides, or that it is
missing).
.Ar model
is a game path such as
.Pa meshes/armor/iron/f/cuirass_1.nif ,
or a
.Pa .nif
file on disk.
This is a software preview for checking shape, texture mapping and colours, not the
game's renderer: no normal, specular or glow maps and no skin or hair tint.
Skyrim LE models are refused.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -views Ar list
Comma-separated views: front, three-quarter, right, back, left, or an angle in degrees.
The default is front, three-quarter, right and back.
.It Fl -size Ar pixels
Width and height of each view; the default is 480.
.It Fl -body
Also draw the installed female body, hands and feet, for scale.
.It Fl -with Ar model
Draw another model as well; can be repeated.
.It Fl -armour Ar text
Draw an armour by name or editor ID, as the load order wears it; can be repeated.
Use
.Ar -
as the model to draw only armours.
.It Fl -elevation Ar degrees
Camera height above the horizon; the default is 6.
.It Fl -zoom Ar factor
1 fits the whole model; larger zooms in.
.It Fl -transparent
Use a transparent background.
.It Fl -no-pose
Draw skinned models as they are stored.
By default they are posed on the game's female skeleton, as the game does: each vertex moves by
the bones it is weighted to, so a model made on a skeleton that differs from the game's (a few
mods' are shifted by a couple of units) comes out where it does in game, next to the pieces made
on the right one.
.El
.It Cm man Op Fl -install
Print this manual page to standard output.
With
.Fl -install ,
write it to
.Pa ../share/man/man1/skyplug.1
relative to the directory holding the
.Nm
binary instead, and print the path written.
.El
.Pp
.Ar plugin
may be the exact filename, the filename in a different case, or the name
without its extension.
.Ar character
matches a player name exactly or by case-insensitive substring.
.Ar save
matches a save's filename with or without
.Pa .ess ,
or an unambiguous substring of it.
An ambiguous match fails and lists the candidates.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -game-dir Ar dir
Use the Skyrim Special Edition install in
.Ar dir
(the directory containing
.Pa SkyrimSE.exe )
instead of searching the Steam libraries.
The Proton prefix is looked up in the Steam library that contains
.Ar dir ;
for a game outside a Steam library, give its prefix with
.Fl -prefix .
A directory holding a
.Pa goggame-*.info
file is GOG's build, whose per-user folders are named
.Pa Skyrim Special Edition GOG .
.It Fl -prefix Ar dir
Read
.Pa Plugins.txt
and the saves from the Wine prefix
.Ar dir
(the directory holding
.Pa drive_c )
instead of the Steam library's Proton prefix, as for GOG's build run
under umu or Wine.
The Windows user inside it is
.Ql steamuser
when that exists, as under Proton and umu, else the Unix user.
.It Fl -appid Ar appid
Steam AppID used to locate the game and its Proton prefix.
Defaults to 489830, Skyrim Special Edition.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print a short usage summary.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev SKYPLUG_GAME_DIR
Used for
.Fl -game-dir
when it isn't given.
.It Ev SKYPLUG_PREFIX
Used for
.Fl -prefix
when it isn't given.
.El
.Sh EDITOR
.Cm edit
has two tabs,
.Sy Plugins
and
.Sy Saves ,
switched with
.Ic tab .
.Pp
In both tabs:
.Bl -tag -width "space, enter" -compact
.It Ic j , k , Ic up , down
move the selection
.It Ic gg , G
jump to the top or bottom
.It Ic tab
switch tab
.It Ic s
save plugin changes and quit
.It Ic q , esc
quit, asking again first if there are unsaved changes
.El
.Pp
In the Plugins tab:
.Bl -tag -width "space, enter" -compact
.It Ic space , enter
toggle the selected plugin
.It Ic /
filter by substring as you type;
.Ic enter
keeps the filter,
.Ic esc
restores the previous one
.It Ic o
cycle the sort order: load order, name, type, enabled
.El
.Pp
Toggles are held in memory and marked with a trailing
.Ql *
until saved with
.Ic s .
Always-loaded and missing plugins cannot be toggled.
.Pp
In the Saves tab, which goes from characters to their saves to a save's
plugins:
.Bl -tag -width "space, enter" -compact
.It Ic l , right , enter
open the selected character or save
.It Ic h , left , backspace
go back up a level
.It Ic esc
go back up a level, or quit at the top
.El
.Pp
A save's plugins are marked against the current setup, including unsaved
toggles, so you can enable what a save needs in the Plugins tab and check
it in the Saves tab before saving.
.Sh FILES
Paths are shown relative to the Steam library holding the game,
.Ar lib ,
and to the Proton user directory inside it,
.Ar user ,
which is
.Pa lib/steamapps/compatdata/489830/pfx/drive_c/users/steamuser
for the default AppID.
With
.Fl -prefix ,
.Ar user
is the user directory in that prefix instead, and for GOG's build the
per-user folders are named
.Pa Skyrim Special Edition GOG .
.Cm paths
prints the resolved ones.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa lib/steamapps/common/Skyrim Special Edition/Data/
Installed plugins.
.It Pa lib/steamapps/common/Skyrim Special Edition/Skyrim.ccc
Creation Club plugins the engine always loads.
.It Pa user/AppData/Local/Skyrim Special Edition/Plugins.txt
The load order.
.Nm
writes
.Pa Plugins.txt.bak
beside it before every change.
.It Pa user/Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/Saves/
Save files.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/Steam , ~/.steam/steam , ~/.steam/root
Steam installs searched for
.Pa libraryfolders.vdf ,
along with the Flatpak install under
.Pa ~/.var/app/com.valvesoftware.Steam .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
List the plugins that are installed but switched off:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ skyplug list | grep '^\e[ \e]'
.Ed
.Pp
Enable a plugin by name, ignoring case and extension:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ skyplug enable "paarthurnax dilemma"
enabled Paarthurnax Dilemma.esp
.Ed
.Pp
Before loading an old save, find which of its mods are missing or
disabled:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ skyplug characters
$ skyplug saves tessta
$ skyplug save-plugins Quicksave0 | grep -v '\e[x\e]'
.Ed
.Pp
Use Skyrim VR, or an install the Steam search does not find:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ skyplug --appid 611670 list
$ skyplug --game-dir "/mnt/games/Skyrim Special Edition" paths
.Ed
.Pp
Use GOG's build, run under umu with its own prefix:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ export SKYPLUG_GAME_DIR="/games/gog/Skyrim Special Edition"
$ export SKYPLUG_PREFIX=/games/gog/prefixes/skyrim-se
$ skyplug list
.Ed
.Pp
Install this page after
.Ql cargo install skyplug ,
or read it without installing:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ skyplug man --install
$ skyplug man | man -l -
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr man 1
